          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "candēla is built on candeō, \"to shine, to glow white\" (Lewis & Short), with -ēla, an ending for a tool. candeō is usually traced to Proto-Indo-European (s)kand-, \"to shine\" (EtymDB 2.1). English candle comes from candēla."
            }
          ]
